      "message": "That\u0027s correct, but I don\u0027t understand why this entry was added, and the other wasn\u0027t (and this caused build breakage).\n\nI\u0027m suspecting that this entry wasn\u0027t needed, and that there was a TH failure (related to LKGB ???) causing keymint to be able to merge without the \u0027-unstable\u0027 library here. Merging this would confirm that.\n\nThe other theory is that:\n- on some builds the variant w/o \"-unstable\" is in the VNDK\n- on other builds the variant w/ \"-unstable\" is in the VNDK\n\nHaving different VNDK definitions per-lunch target would be a problem (and at least 1-2 other HALs have added both here, I just don\u0027t understand why - I don\u0027t think they need to). SO - if this doesn\u0027t cause any build breakage, then it\u0027s just overly cautious adds to this list (and we can relax). If it does, then it identifies a bug in the VNDK.",
